./docs/sound.md:1:# Sound
./docs/sound.md:2:Sound is a game requirement that keeps Neon Pairs silent.
./docs/sound.md:6:You can play in a shared room without starting audio. Card feedback and completion are conveyed by the game display and accessible announcements.
./docs/sound.md:10:- S01 - Keep the game silent for every action and state, including a reveal, a match, a mismatch, a restart and a win.
./docs/sound.md:12:- S02 - Include no audio files, audio API calls or sound toggle in this version. Silence is the required behavior, not an unfinished feature.
./docs/architecture.md:12:- A02 - Keep the board description and deck immutable. Keep matched positions, current selection, moves, active elapsed milliseconds and whether play started in game state. Derive pair count and victory. Serialize progress using the [reproducibility formats](reproducibility.md).
./docs/architecture.md:14:- A03 - Use direct calls and exhaustive branches for the closed, one-card and mismatch states. Keep named states, format versions, timing values and size limits beside the behavior they control.
